{"files":[{"content":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    long int start;\n    long int total;\n    long int next;\n} bucket;\n\nstatic char *sort_strings;\nstatic int sort_length;\n\nstatic int compare_indices(const void *left, const void *right) {\n    long int a = *(const long int *)left;\n    long int b = *(const long int *)right;\n\n    return strcmp(sort_strings + a * sort_length,\n                  sort_strings + b * sort_length);\n}\n\nlong int *bucket_sort(char *a, int length, long int size, int offset,\n                      int nbuckets) {\n    long int *returns = malloc(sizeof(*returns) * (size > 0 ? size : 1));\n    bucket *buckets = calloc((size_t)nbuckets, sizeof(*buckets));\n    long int i;\n    long int prefix = 0;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        int bucket_index = (unsigned char)a[i * length] - offset;\n        buckets[bucket_index].total++;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++) {\n        buckets[i].start = prefix;\n        buckets[i].next = prefix;\n        prefix += buckets[i].total;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        int bucket_index = (unsigned char)a[i * length] - offset;\n        buckets[bucket_index].next++;\n        returns[buckets[bucket_index].next - 1] = i;\n    }\n\n    sort_strings = a;\n    sort_length = length;\n\n    /* Each bucket owns a disjoint index range; the histogram and scatter\n       above remain serial because multiple elements can update one bucket. */\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic, 1) if (size > (long int)nbuckets * 64)\n    for (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++) {\n        qsort(returns + buckets[i].start, (size_t)buckets[i].total,\n              sizeof(*returns), compare_indices);\n    }\n\n    free(buckets);\n    return returns;\n}\n\nvoid load(char **vString, long int *N, int *l, int *os, int *nb) {\n    char *strings = NULL;\n    int len;\n    int offset;\n    int nbucket;\n    long int n;\n    long int i;\n\n    if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &len)) {\n        printf(\"ERROR len\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%ld\", &n)) {\n        printf(\"ERROR n\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &offset)) {\n        printf(\"ERROR offset\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &nbucket)) {\n        printf(\"ERROR nbucket\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    nbucket = nbucket + 1;\n    len = len + 1;\n\n    strings = (char *)malloc(n * len);\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%s\", strings + (i * len))) {\n            printf(\"ERROR %ld\\n\", i);\n            exit(1);\n        }\n    }\n\n    *vString = strings;\n    *N = n;\n    *l = len;\n    *os = offset;\n    *nb = nbucket;\n}\n\nvoid print(char *strings, long int *index, long int n, int len) {\n    long int i;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        printf(\"%ld -> %s\\n\", i, strings + (index[i] * len));\n    }\n}\n\nvoid save(char *strings, long int *index, long int n, int len) {\n    long int i;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        printf(\"%s\\n\", strings + (index[i] * len));\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int ac, char **av) {\n    char *strings = NULL;\n    long int N = 0;\n    long int *index = NULL;\n    int len = 0;\n    int offset;\n    int nbuckets;\n\n    load(&strings, &N, &len, &offset, &nbuckets);\n\n    index = bucket_sort(strings, len, N, offset, nbuckets);\n\n    save(strings, index, N, len);\n\n    if (strings != NULL)\n        free(strings);\n\n    if (index != NULL)\n        free(index);\n\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n","path":"src/bucketsort.c"}],"hypothesis":"Replacing insertion sort's loop-carried shifts with qsort should avoid quadratic work for disordered buckets. After counting and prefixing, each bucket owns a disjoint index range, so sorting those ranges in parallel is race-free; bucket counting and scatter remain serial because their updates can collide.","notes":"One source-only experiment. The OpenMP parallel loop uses a size-based guard to limit small-input overhead. No measurements were made; correctness and performance remain for the controller to evaluate.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Count bucket sizes and use prefix offsets for correctly sized, disjoint storage instead of fixed equal-sized slices.","Replace dependent insertion-sort shifts with qsort for each bucket.","Parallelize independent bucket sorts with a dynamically scheduled OpenMP loop; leave potentially conflicting histogram and scatter updates serial."]}